From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jahred Love <jahred.love@aircall.io>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:52:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Check the input of the description, candidate and signalling
 parsers

What: the remote description parser copied each line into a 256-byte
buffer without a bound, and the ICE ufrag, password and fingerprint with
unbounded strncpy. Candidates were read with unbounded sscanf into fixed
fields, past the end of their own line, and at most 10 remote candidates
were kept, the 11th written past the array. Signalling copied the URL's
host and path and the token into fixed fields without a bound or a
terminating zero, read the WHIP answer and MQTT messages as if they ended
in a zero byte, and dereferenced a missing JSON-RPC method.

Now every line is read where it lies, however long; each field is checked
against what it goes into and refused, never cut short; up to 32 remote
candidates are kept (AGENT_MAX_REMOTE_CANDIDATES) and one more is an
error, with candidate pairs bounded to match. The parsers return 0 or an
ICE_ERROR_ code, and a description that is refused changes nothing.
Candidates libpeer cannot use, such as TCP ones, are still passed over in
a description. peer_signaling_connect returns -1 for a URL or token that
is malformed or too long.

Why: wobblertc hands libpeer descriptions and candidates from remote peers
and signalling servers, which must not be able to overflow its buffers.

Like libpeer, this patch is under the MIT licence.
